---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { Circle, ArrowUp, Zap, Grid3x3, Check, Ban, Flame, ArrowUpFromLine, Cable, RefreshCw, ArrowLeftRight, Trophy, Lightbulb } from 'lucide-astro';
---

<Layout title="Rules | Matt's Volleyball" description="Official rules for Matt's Volleyball sand volleyball leagues in Lake Norman. Game rules, serving, spiking, net play, substitutions, and playoffs.">
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="bg-gradient-to-br from-ocean-600 to-ocean-800 text-white pt-20 md:pt-28">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center">
      <h1 class="font-display font-black text-4xl sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl mb-4">Rules</h1>
      <p class="text-white/80 text-lg md:text-xl max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        Know the rules. Play fair. Have fun.
      </p>
    </div>
    <svg viewBox="0 0 1440 80" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-full">
      <path d="M0 40C360 80 720 0 1080 40C1260 60 1380 50 1440 40V80H0V40Z" fill="#F7F6F3" />
    </svg>
  </section>

  <section class="py-12 md:py-20">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="space-y-12">

        <!-- THE GAME -->
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-display font-extrabold text-2xl md:text-3xl text-ocean-600 mb-6 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-10 h-10 bg-ocean-600 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center text-white">
              <Circle class="w-5 h-5" />
            </span>
            The Game
          </h2>
          <ul class="space-y-4 text-ocean-700 leading-relaxed list-none pl-0">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 text-ocean-500" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M19.04 4.85C17.34 3.2 15.33 2.25 13 2v3.62l9 5.18c-.28-2.3-1.27-4.3-2.96-5.95M12 22c3.44 0 6.16-1.38 8.17-4.14L17.06 16l-8.99 5.2c1.25.53 2.57.8 3.93.8m1-10.59l8.15 4.66c.44-.94.73-1.93.85-2.96l-9-5.18zm-9.12 6.4c.66.91 1.38 1.65 2.17 2.19l8.99-5.1L12 13.15zM11.04 2C10 2.09 9 2.36 8 2.8v10.35l3.04-1.74zM2 12c0 1.39.3 2.77.89 4.12L6 14.28V4c-2.67 2-4 4.65-4 8"/></svg>
              <span><strong>Starting at the scheduled game time,</strong> or as soon as the court is free, if the previous match ran long, whichever team is first to have its full roster on the court gets to choose the serve or the side of the court. If both teams are full at the same moment, rock/paper/scissors decides.</span>
            </li>

            <li>
              <div class="bg-ocean-600/5 border-l-4 border-ocean-500 px-5 py-4 rounded-r-lg">
                <p class="font-semibold text-ocean-800 mb-2">Game Time Limit</p>
                <p>All matches have a maximum time limit of <strong>1 hour</strong>. The scheduled game time serves as the start time for each match. If a match is scheduled for 6:30 PM, the set must be completed by 7:30 PM regardless of the score or whether all 3 sets have been fully played. One hour after the scheduled game time, teams must immediately leave the court, and the score at that time will be recorded as the final score. No exceptions will be made to extend matches beyond the 1-hour time limit.</p>
              </div>
            </li>

            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 text-ocean-500" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M19.04 4.85C17.34 3.2 15.33 2.25 13 2v3.62l9 5.18c-.28-2.3-1.27-4.3-2.96-5.95M12 22c3.44 0 6.16-1.38 8.17-4.14L17.06 16l-8.99 5.2c1.25.53 2.57.8 3.93.8m1-10.59l8.15 4.66c.44-.94.73-1.93.85-2.96l-9-5.18zm-9.12 6.4c.66.91 1.38 1.65 2.17 2.19l8.99-5.1L12 13.15zM11.04 2C10 2.09 9 2.36 8 2.8v10.35l3.04-1.74zM2 12c0 1.39.3 2.77.89 4.12L6 14.28V4c-2.67 2-4 4.65-4 8"/></svg>
              <span><strong>Game time is forfeit time.</strong> Start playing at your scheduled game time, even if your full team isn't present.</span>
            </li>

            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 text-ocean-500" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M19.04 4.85C17.34 3.2 15.33 2.25 13 2v3.62l9 5.18c-.28-2.3-1.27-4.3-2.96-5.95M12 22c3.44 0 6.16-1.38 8.17-4.14L17.06 16l-8.99 5.2c1.25.53 2.57.8 3.93.8m1-10.59l8.15 4.66c.44-.94.73-1.93.85-2.96l-9-5.18zm-9.12 6.4c.66.91 1.38 1.65 2.17 2.19l8.99-5.1L12 13.15zM11.04 2C10 2.09 9 2.36 8 2.8v10.35l3.04-1.74zM2 12c0 1.39.3 2.77.89 4.12L6 14.28V4c-2.67 2-4 4.65-4 8"/></svg>
              <span>The best of three sets will win matches. Each set will be won by the team that first scores <strong>21 points, straight up</strong>. All three sets will be played during the regular season.</span>
            </li>

            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 text-ocean-500" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M19.04 4.85C17.34 3.2 15.33 2.25 13 2v3.62l9 5.18c-.28-2.3-1.27-4.3-2.96-5.95M12 22c3.44 0 6.16-1.38 8.17-4.14L17.06 16l-8.99 5.2c1.25.53 2.57.8 3.93.8m1-10.59l8.15 4.66c.44-.94.73-1.93.85-2.96l-9-5.18zm-9.12 6.4c.66.91 1.38 1.65 2.17 2.19l8.99-5.1L12 13.15zM11.04 2C10 2.09 9 2.36 8 2.8v10.35l3.04-1.74zM2 12c0 1.39.3 2.77.89 4.12L6 14.28V4c-2.67 2-4 4.65-4 8"/></svg>
              <span>In the <strong>3rd set</strong>, teams switch sides of the court as soon as either team reaches <strong>11 points</strong>.</span>
            </li>

            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 text-ocean-500" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M19.04 4.85C17.34 3.2 15.33 2.25 13 2v3.62l9 5.18c-.28-2.3-1.27-4.3-2.96-5.95M12 22c3.44 0 6.16-1.38 8.17-4.14L17.06 16l-8.99 5.2c1.25.53 2.57.8 3.93.8m1-10.59l8.15 4.66c.44-.94.73-1.93.85-2.96l-9-5.18zm-9.12 6.4c.66.91 1.38 1.65 2.17 2.19l8.99-5.1L12 13.15zM11.04 2C10 2.09 9 2.36 8 2.8v10.35l3.04-1.74zM2 12c0 1.39.3 2.77.89 4.12L6 14.28V4c-2.67 2-4 4.65-4 8"/></svg>
              <span>Each team is permitted <strong>1 thirty-second team time-out per set</strong>.</span>
            </li>

            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 text-ocean-500" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M19.04 4.85C17.34 3.2 15.33 2.25 13 2v3.62l9 5.18c-.28-2.3-1.27-4.3-2.96-5.95M12 22c3.44 0 6.16-1.38 8.17-4.14L17.06 16l-8.99 5.2c1.25.53 2.57.8 3.93.8m1-10.59l8.15 4.66c.44-.94.73-1.93.85-2.96l-9-5.18zm-9.12 6.4c.66.91 1.38 1.65 2.17 2.19l8.99-5.1L12 13.15zM11.04 2C10 2.09 9 2.36 8 2.8v10.35l3.04-1.74zM2 12c0 1.39.3 2.77.89 4.12L6 14.28V4c-2.67 2-4 4.65-4 8"/></svg>
              <span>Rest periods between sets of a match shall be no longer than <strong>2 minutes</strong>. Be respectful of everyone's time. This is not the time to go inside and order more drinks. Do not leave the immediate playing area.</span>
            </li>

            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 text-ocean-500" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M19.04 4.85C17.34 3.2 15.33 2.25 13 2v3.62l9 5.18c-.28-2.3-1.27-4.3-2.96-5.95M12 22c3.44 0 6.16-1.38 8.17-4.14L17.06 16l-8.99 5.2c1.25.53 2.57.8 3.93.8m1-10.59l8.15 4.66c.44-.94.73-1.93.85-2.96l-9-5.18zm-9.12 6.4c.66.91 1.38 1.65 2.17 2.19l8.99-5.1L12 13.15zM11.04 2C10 2.09 9 2.36 8 2.8v10.35l3.04-1.74zM2 12c0 1.39.3 2.77.89 4.12L6 14.28V4c-2.67 2-4 4.65-4 8"/></svg>
              <span>Point will be scored on each rally. If the receiving team wins the rally, they score a point and gain the serve.</span>
            </li>

            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 text-ocean-500" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M19.04 4.85C17.34 3.2 15.33 2.25 13 2v3.62l9 5.18c-.28-2.3-1.27-4.3-2.96-5.95M12 22c3.44 0 6.16-1.38 8.17-4.14L17.06 16l-8.99 5.2c1.25.53 2.57.8 3.93.8m1-10.59l8.15 4.66c.44-.94.73-1.93.85-2.96l-9-5.18zm-9.12 6.4c.66.91 1.38 1.65 2.17 2.19l8.99-5.1L12 13.15zM11.04 2C10 2.09 9 2.36 8 2.8v10.35l3.04-1.74zM2 12c0 1.39.3 2.77.89 4.12L6 14.28V4c-2.67 2-4 4.65-4 8"/></svg>
              <span>Games are self-reffed, and you must keep your own score. Captains can submit scores through the TeamLinkt app or website.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- THE SERVE -->
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-display font-extrabold text-2xl md:text-3xl text-ocean-600 mb-6 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-10 h-10 bg-ocean-500 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center text-white">
              <ArrowUp class="w-5 h-5" />
            </span>
            The Serve
          </h2>
          <ul class="space-y-4 text-ocean-700 leading-relaxed list-none pl-0">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 text-ocean-500" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M19.04 4.85C17.34 3.2 15.33 2.25 13 2v3.62l9 5.18c-.28-2.3-1.27-4.3-2.96-5.95M12 22c3.44 0 6.16-1.38 8.17-4.14L17.06 16l-8.99 5.2c1.25.53 2.57.8 3.93.8m1-10.59l8.15 4.66c.44-.94.73-1.93.85-2.96l-9-5.18zm-9.12 6.4c.66.91 1.38 1.65 2.17 2.19l8.99-5.1L12 13.15zM11.04 2C10 2.09 9 2.36 8 2.8v10.35l3.04-1.74zM2 12c0 1.39.3 2.77.89 4.12L6 14.28V4c-2.67 2-4 4.65-4 8"/></svg>
              <span>The service zone includes the full width of the rear boundary line. The server may move freely within the service zone. At the moment of the service hit or takeoff for a jump service, the server must be completely in the service zone and not touching the court (end line included).</span>
            </li>

            <li>
              <div class="bg-ocean-600/5 border-l-4 border-ocean-500 px-5 py-4 rounded-r-lg">
                <p class="font-semibold text-ocean-800 mb-2">Net Serve Is In Play</p>
                <p>A served ball that hits the net does not result in the service team losing its serve. The net serve is considered in-play, unless 1) it does not continue over the net or 2) lands outside the opposing team's court-side untouched by the opposing team.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- SPIKING & BLOCKING -->
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-display font-extrabold text-2xl md:text-3xl text-ocean-600 mb-6 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-10 h-10 bg-ocean-600 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center text-white">
              <Zap class="w-5 h-5" />
            </span>
            Spiking & Blocking
          </h2>
          <ul class="space-y-4 text-ocean-700 leading-relaxed list-none pl-0">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 text-ocean-500" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M19.04 4.85C17.34 3.2 15.33 2.25 13 2v3.62l9 5.18c-.28-2.3-1.27-4.3-2.96-5.95M12 22c3.44 0 6.16-1.38 8.17-4.14L17.06 16l-8.99 5.2c1.25.53 2.57.8 3.93.8m1-10.59l8.15 4.66c.44-.94.73-1.93.85-2.96l-9-5.18zm-9.12 6.4c.66.91 1.38 1.65 2.17 2.19l8.99-5.1L12 13.15zM11.04 2C10 2.09 9 2.36 8 2.8v10.35l3.04-1.74zM2 12c0 1.39.3 2.77.89 4.12L6 14.28V4c-2.67 2-4 4.65-4 8"/></svg>
              <span>The receiving team is <strong>not allowed to block or spike a served ball</strong>.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 text-ocean-500" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M19.04 4.85C17.34 3.2 15.33 2.25 13 2v3.62l9 5.18c-.28-2.3-1.27-4.3-2.96-5.95M12 22c3.44 0 6.16-1.38 8.17-4.14L17.06 16l-8.99 5.2c1.25.53 2.57.8 3.93.8m1-10.59l8.15 4.66c.44-.94.73-1.93.85-2.96l-9-5.18zm-9.12 6.4c.66.91 1.38 1.65 2.17 2.19l8.99-5.1L12 13.15zM11.04 2C10 2.09 9 2.36 8 2.8v10.35l3.04-1.74zM2 12c0 1.39.3 2.77.89 4.12L6 14.28V4c-2.67 2-4 4.65-4 8"/></svg>
              <span>A spiker must contact the ball on his/her own side of the net, but may in the course of the follow through reach over (but not touch) the net.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 text-ocean-500" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M19.04 4.85C17.34 3.2 15.33 2.25 13 2v3.62l9 5.18c-.28-2.3-1.27-4.3-2.96-5.95M12 22c3.44 0 6.16-1.38 8.17-4.14L17.06 16l-8.99 5.2c1.25.53 2.57.8 3.93.8m1-10.59l8.15 4.66c.44-.94.73-1.93.85-2.96l-9-5.18zm-9.12 6.4c.66.91 1.38 1.65 2.17 2.19l8.99-5.1L12 13.15zM11.04 2C10 2.09 9 2.36 8 2.8v10.35l3.04-1.74zM2 12c0 1.39.3 2.77.89 4.12L6 14.28V4c-2.67 2-4 4.65-4 8"/></svg>
              <span>The team that has affected the block shall have the right to three more contacts, with the blocker having the right to make the first of the three allowable hits.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- NET PLAY -->
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-display font-extrabold text-2xl md:text-3xl text-ocean-600 mb-6 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-10 h-10 bg-sand-500 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center text-white">
              <Grid3x3 class="w-5 h-5" />
            </span>
            Net Play
          </h2>
          <ul class="space-y-4 text-ocean-700 leading-relaxed list-none pl-0">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 text-ocean-500" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M19.04 4.85C17.34 3.2 15.33 2.25 13 2v3.62l9 5.18c-.28-2.3-1.27-4.3-2.96-5.95M12 22c3.44 0 6.16-1.38 8.17-4.14L17.06 16l-8.99 5.2c1.25.53 2.57.8 3.93.8m1-10.59l8.15 4.66c.44-.94.73-1.93.85-2.96l-9-5.18zm-9.12 6.4c.66.91 1.38 1.65 2.17 2.19l8.99-5.1L12 13.15zM11.04 2C10 2.09 9 2.36 8 2.8v10.35l3.04-1.74zM2 12c0 1.39.3 2.77.89 4.12L6 14.28V4c-2.67 2-4 4.65-4 8"/></svg>
              <span>A ball hit into the net may still be kept in play (up to 3 hits) provided that a player does not make contact with the net.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 text-ocean-500" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M19.04 4.85C17.34 3.2 15.33 2.25 13 2v3.62l9 5.18c-.28-2.3-1.27-4.3-2.96-5.95M12 22c3.44 0 6.16-1.38 8.17-4.14L17.06 16l-8.99 5.2c1.25.53 2.57.8 3.93.8m1-10.59l8.15 4.66c.44-.94.73-1.93.85-2.96l-9-5.18zm-9.12 6.4c.66.91 1.38 1.65 2.17 2.19l8.99-5.1L12 13.15zM11.04 2C10 2.09 9 2.36 8 2.8v10.35l3.04-1.74zM2 12c0 1.39.3 2.77.89 4.12L6 14.28V4c-2.67 2-4 4.65-4 8"/></svg>
              <span><strong>Players may not touch the net.</strong> If 2 opposing players touch the net simultaneously, the ball is declared dead and the point is replayed.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- LEGAL PLAY -->
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-display font-extrabold text-2xl md:text-3xl text-ocean-600 mb-6 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-10 h-10 bg-ocean-500 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center text-white">
              <Check class="w-5 h-5" />
            </span>
            Legal Play
          </h2>
          <ul class="space-y-4 text-ocean-700 leading-relaxed list-none pl-0">
            <li>
              <div class="bg-ocean-600/5 border-l-4 border-ocean-500 px-5 py-4 rounded-r-lg">
                <p class="font-semibold text-ocean-800 mb-2">You Can Use Any Part of Your Body</p>
                <p>New to sand volleyball? You are allowed to play the ball off <strong>any part of your body</strong>, not just your hands and arms. Feet, legs, head, chest, whatever it takes to keep the rally alive is legal, as long as the ball rebounds cleanly.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 text-ocean-500" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M19.04 4.85C17.34 3.2 15.33 2.25 13 2v3.62l9 5.18c-.28-2.3-1.27-4.3-2.96-5.95M12 22c3.44 0 6.16-1.38 8.17-4.14L17.06 16l-8.99 5.2c1.25.53 2.57.8 3.93.8m1-10.59l8.15 4.66c.44-.94.73-1.93.85-2.96l-9-5.18zm-9.12 6.4c.66.91 1.38 1.65 2.17 2.19l8.99-5.1L12 13.15zM11.04 2C10 2.09 9 2.36 8 2.8v10.35l3.04-1.74zM2 12c0 1.39.3 2.77.89 4.12L6 14.28V4c-2.67 2-4 4.65-4 8"/></svg>
              <span>The ball must be returned over the net in <strong>3 hits or less</strong>.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 text-ocean-500" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M19.04 4.85C17.34 3.2 15.33 2.25 13 2v3.62l9 5.18c-.28-2.3-1.27-4.3-2.96-5.95M12 22c3.44 0 6.16-1.38 8.17-4.14L17.06 16l-8.99 5.2c1.25.53 2.57.8 3.93.8m1-10.59l8.15 4.66c.44-.94.73-1.93.85-2.96l-9-5.18zm-9.12 6.4c.66.91 1.38 1.65 2.17 2.19l8.99-5.1L12 13.15zM11.04 2C10 2.09 9 2.36 8 2.8v10.35l3.04-1.74zM2 12c0 1.39.3 2.77.89 4.12L6 14.28V4c-2.67 2-4 4.65-4 8"/></svg>
              <span>It is legal to contact the ball with <strong>any part of the body</strong> as long as the ball rebounds immediately. It may not "lay" against the body. If a player touches the ball or the ball touches a player, it is considered as a play on the ball. Except in the following case: A ball touching the body more than once in succession is legal when played off a hard-driven spiked ball, or blocked and played again by the blocker.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 text-ocean-500" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M19.04 4.85C17.34 3.2 15.33 2.25 13 2v3.62l9 5.18c-.28-2.3-1.27-4.3-2.96-5.95M12 22c3.44 0 6.16-1.38 8.17-4.14L17.06 16l-8.99 5.2c1.25.53 2.57.8 3.93.8m1-10.59l8.15 4.66c.44-.94.73-1.93.85-2.96l-9-5.18zm-9.12 6.4c.66.91 1.38 1.65 2.17 2.19l8.99-5.1L12 13.15zM11.04 2C10 2.09 9 2.36 8 2.8v10.35l3.04-1.74zM2 12c0 1.39.3 2.77.89 4.12L6 14.28V4c-2.67 2-4 4.65-4 8"/></svg>
              <span>If 2 players on the same team contact the ball simultaneously, it counts as <strong>one</strong> contact, and any player may play the ball.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 text-ocean-500" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M19.04 4.85C17.34 3.2 15.33 2.25 13 2v3.62l9 5.18c-.28-2.3-1.27-4.3-2.96-5.95M12 22c3.44 0 6.16-1.38 8.17-4.14L17.06 16l-8.99 5.2c1.25.53 2.57.8 3.93.8m1-10.59l8.15 4.66c.44-.94.73-1.93.85-2.96l-9-5.18zm-9.12 6.4c.66.91 1.38 1.65 2.17 2.19l8.99-5.1L12 13.15zM11.04 2C10 2.09 9 2.36 8 2.8v10.35l3.04-1.74zM2 12c0 1.39.3 2.77.89 4.12L6 14.28V4c-2.67 2-4 4.65-4 8"/></svg>
              <span>One may play the ball twice during a volley, but not twice in succession, <strong>unless played directly off a block</strong>.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 text-ocean-500" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M19.04 4.85C17.34 3.2 15.33 2.25 13 2v3.62l9 5.18c-.28-2.3-1.27-4.3-2.96-5.95M12 22c3.44 0 6.16-1.38 8.17-4.14L17.06 16l-8.99 5.2c1.25.53 2.57.8 3.93.8m1-10.59l8.15 4.66c.44-.94.73-1.93.85-2.96l-9-5.18zm-9.12 6.4c.66.91 1.38 1.65 2.17 2.19l8.99-5.1L12 13.15zM11.04 2C10 2.09 9 2.36 8 2.8v10.35l3.04-1.74zM2 12c0 1.39.3 2.77.89 4.12L6 14.28V4c-2.67 2-4 4.65-4 8"/></svg>
              <span>When a ball touches a boundary line, it is considered <strong>in play</strong>.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- ILLEGAL PLAY -->
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-display font-extrabold text-2xl md:text-3xl text-ocean-600 mb-6 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-10 h-10 bg-ocean-700 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center text-white">
              <Ban class="w-5 h-5" />
            </span>
            Illegal Play
          </h2>
          <ul class="space-y-4 text-ocean-700 leading-relaxed list-none pl-0">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 text-ocean-500" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M19.04 4.85C17.34 3.2 15.33 2.25 13 2v3.62l9 5.18c-.28-2.3-1.27-4.3-2.96-5.95M12 22c3.44 0 6.16-1.38 8.17-4.14L17.06 16l-8.99 5.2c1.25.53 2.57.8 3.93.8m1-10.59l8.15 4.66c.44-.94.73-1.93.85-2.96l-9-5.18zm-9.12 6.4c.66.91 1.38 1.65 2.17 2.19l8.99-5.1L12 13.15zM11.04 2C10 2.09 9 2.36 8 2.8v10.35l3.04-1.74zM2 12c0 1.39.3 2.77.89 4.12L6 14.28V4c-2.67 2-4 4.65-4 8"/></svg>
              <span>Players are not permitted to scoop, hold, and lift or push the ball. <strong>The ball may never be contacted with an open-hand underhanded motion.</strong></span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- COMPETITIVE DIVISIONS -->
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-display font-extrabold text-2xl md:text-3xl text-ocean-600 mb-6 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-10 h-10 bg-ocean-600 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center text-white">
              <Flame class="w-5 h-5" />
            </span>
            Extra Rules for Competitive Divisions
          </h2>
          <ul class="space-y-4 text-ocean-700 leading-relaxed list-none pl-0">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 text-ocean-500" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M19.04 4.85C17.34 3.2 15.33 2.25 13 2v3.62l9 5.18c-.28-2.3-1.27-4.3-2.96-5.95M12 22c3.44 0 6.16-1.38 8.17-4.14L17.06 16l-8.99 5.2c1.25.53 2.57.8 3.93.8m1-10.59l8.15 4.66c.44-.94.73-1.93.85-2.96l-9-5.18zm-9.12 6.4c.66.91 1.38 1.65 2.17 2.19l8.99-5.1L12 13.15zM11.04 2C10 2.09 9 2.36 8 2.8v10.35l3.04-1.74zM2 12c0 1.39.3 2.77.89 4.12L6 14.28V4c-2.67 2-4 4.65-4 8"/></svg>
              <span><strong>No open-handed receiving</strong> (fingertips), except on hard-driven balls. The motion should be REACTIONARY.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 text-ocean-500" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M19.04 4.85C17.34 3.2 15.33 2.25 13 2v3.62l9 5.18c-.28-2.3-1.27-4.3-2.96-5.95M12 22c3.44 0 6.16-1.38 8.17-4.14L17.06 16l-8.99 5.2c1.25.53 2.57.8 3.93.8m1-10.59l8.15 4.66c.44-.94.73-1.93.85-2.96l-9-5.18zm-9.12 6.4c.66.91 1.38 1.65 2.17 2.19l8.99-5.1L12 13.15zM11.04 2C10 2.09 9 2.36 8 2.8v10.35l3.04-1.74zM2 12c0 1.39.3 2.77.89 4.12L6 14.28V4c-2.67 2-4 4.65-4 8"/></svg>
              <span>Hand sets must be <strong>clean, with little or no rotation</strong> on the ball. Elbows should be extending out when you contact the ball.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 text-ocean-500" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M19.04 4.85C17.34 3.2 15.33 2.25 13 2v3.62l9 5.18c-.28-2.3-1.27-4.3-2.96-5.95M12 22c3.44 0 6.16-1.38 8.17-4.14L17.06 16l-8.99 5.2c1.25.53 2.57.8 3.93.8m1-10.59l8.15 4.66c.44-.94.73-1.93.85-2.96l-9-5.18zm-9.12 6.4c.66.91 1.38 1.65 2.17 2.19l8.99-5.1L12 13.15zM11.04 2C10 2.09 9 2.36 8 2.8v10.35l3.04-1.74zM2 12c0 1.39.3 2.77.89 4.12L6 14.28V4c-2.67 2-4 4.65-4 8"/></svg>
              <span><strong>No overhand sets over the net.</strong> Hand sets must be directed to a teammate; you cannot send an overhand set across the net regardless of shoulder alignment.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 text-ocean-500" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M19.04 4.85C17.34 3.2 15.33 2.25 13 2v3.62l9 5.18c-.28-2.3-1.27-4.3-2.96-5.95M12 22c3.44 0 6.16-1.38 8.17-4.14L17.06 16l-8.99 5.2c1.25.53 2.57.8 3.93.8m1-10.59l8.15 4.66c.44-.94.73-1.93.85-2.96l-9-5.18zm-9.12 6.4c.66.91 1.38 1.65 2.17 2.19l8.99-5.1L12 13.15zM11.04 2C10 2.09 9 2.36 8 2.8v10.35l3.04-1.74zM2 12c0 1.39.3 2.77.89 4.12L6 14.28V4c-2.67 2-4 4.65-4 8"/></svg>
              <span><strong>No open-handed tipping, dinking, or dunking.</strong> Players who contact the ball with one hand and are putting the ball over the net must cleanly hit with the heel or palm of hand (a roll shot), with straight, locked fingers and a locked wrist (a cobra), knurled fingers (a camel toe), or with the back of the hand (locked wrist and locked fingers/knuckles). One-handed placement or redirection of the ball with the fingers (dink or open-handed tip) is a fault.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- SKYBALL -->
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-display font-extrabold text-2xl md:text-3xl text-ocean-600 mb-6 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-10 h-10 bg-sand-400 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center text-white">
              <ArrowUpFromLine class="w-5 h-5" />
            </span>
            Skyball for the Win
          </h2>
          <ul class="space-y-4 text-ocean-700 leading-relaxed list-none pl-0">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 text-ocean-500" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M19.04 4.85C17.34 3.2 15.33 2.25 13 2v3.62l9 5.18c-.28-2.3-1.27-4.3-2.96-5.95M12 22c3.44 0 6.16-1.38 8.17-4.14L17.06 16l-8.99 5.2c1.25.53 2.57.8 3.93.8m1-10.59l8.15 4.66c.44-.94.73-1.93.85-2.96l-9-5.18zm-9.12 6.4c.66.91 1.38 1.65 2.17 2.19l8.99-5.1L12 13.15zM11.04 2C10 2.09 9 2.36 8 2.8v10.35l3.04-1.74zM2 12c0 1.39.3 2.77.89 4.12L6 14.28V4c-2.67 2-4 4.65-4 8"/></svg>
              <span>Not a requirement, just a tradition. On the possible winning point, if the serving team is up by at least 2 points (i.e. score of 20 to 18), the server should serve the ball as high as possible.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- POWER LINE -->
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-display font-extrabold text-2xl md:text-3xl text-ocean-600 mb-6 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-10 h-10 bg-ocean-600 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center text-white">
              <Cable class="w-5 h-5" />
            </span>
            Power Line
          </h2>
          <ul class="space-y-4 text-ocean-700 leading-relaxed list-none pl-0">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 text-ocean-500" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M19.04 4.85C17.34 3.2 15.33 2.25 13 2v3.62l9 5.18c-.28-2.3-1.27-4.3-2.96-5.95M12 22c3.44 0 6.16-1.38 8.17-4.14L17.06 16l-8.99 5.2c1.25.53 2.57.8 3.93.8m1-10.59l8.15 4.66c.44-.94.73-1.93.85-2.96l-9-5.18zm-9.12 6.4c.66.91 1.38 1.65 2.17 2.19l8.99-5.1L12 13.15zM11.04 2C10 2.09 9 2.36 8 2.8v10.35l3.04-1.74zM2 12c0 1.39.3 2.77.89 4.12L6 14.28V4c-2.67 2-4 4.65-4 8"/></svg>
              <span>A ball hitting the power line above a playable area shall remain in play provided the ball contacts the power line on the side of the net that is occupied by the team that last played the ball.</span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <div class="bg-ocean-600/5 border-l-4 border-ocean-500 px-5 py-4 rounded-r-lg">
                <p class="mb-2">If your team hits the ball into the power line <strong>on your side</strong> of the court, <strong>keep playing</strong>.</p>
                <p>If your team hits the ball into the power line on the <strong>OTHER side</strong> of the court, the play is dead, and your team <strong>loses the point</strong>.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- LIGHTS OUT -->
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-display font-extrabold text-2xl md:text-3xl text-ocean-600 mb-6 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-10 h-10 bg-ocean-700 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center text-white">
              <Lightbulb class="w-5 h-5" />
            </span>
            Lights Out
          </h2>
          <ul class="space-y-4 text-ocean-700 leading-relaxed list-none pl-0">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 text-ocean-500" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M19.04 4.85C17.34 3.2 15.33 2.25 13 2v3.62l9 5.18c-.28-2.3-1.27-4.3-2.96-5.95M12 22c3.44 0 6.16-1.38 8.17-4.14L17.06 16l-8.99 5.2c1.25.53 2.57.8 3.93.8m1-10.59l8.15 4.66c.44-.94.73-1.93.85-2.96l-9-5.18zm-9.12 6.4c.66.91 1.38 1.65 2.17 2.19l8.99-5.1L12 13.15zM11.04 2C10 2.09 9 2.36 8 2.8v10.35l3.04-1.74zM2 12c0 1.39.3 2.77.89 4.12L6 14.28V4c-2.67 2-4 4.65-4 8"/></svg>
              <span>The park's stadium lights are on a timer and shut off at a scheduled time each night. The court lights stay off as long as the park lights are bright enough, then automatically turn on once it gets dark. When the park lights cut out, there is a brief 2-second darkness before the court lights come on. If a point is actively in play when the lights go out, <strong>replay the point</strong>. It is not fair to lose a point to the darkness.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- FEMALE AND ROTATION -->
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-display font-extrabold text-2xl md:text-3xl text-ocean-600 mb-6 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-10 h-10 bg-ocean-600 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center text-white">
              <RefreshCw class="w-5 h-5" />
            </span>
            Female & Rotation Requirement
          </h2>
          <div class="overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse">
              <thead>
                <tr class="border-b-2 border-sand-300">
                  <th class="py-3 pr-4 font-display font-bold text-ocean-600">Format</th>
                  <th class="py-3 pr-4 font-display font-bold text-ocean-600">Females Required</th>
                  <th class="py-3 font-display font-bold text-ocean-600">Rotation</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody class="text-ocean-700">
                <tr class="border-b border-sand-200">
                  <td class="py-3 pr-4 font-semibold">5s</td>
                  <td class="py-3 pr-4">2 on the court</td>
                  <td class="py-3">Required on serve</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-sand-200">
                  <td class="py-3 pr-4 font-semibold">4s</td>
                  <td class="py-3 pr-4">1 on the court</td>
                  <td class="py-3">No requirement</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-sand-200">
                  <td class="py-3 pr-4 font-semibold">3s</td>
                  <td class="py-3 pr-4">1 on the court</td>
                  <td class="py-3">No requirement</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="py-3 pr-4 font-semibold">2s</td>
                  <td class="py-3 pr-4">None</td>
                  <td class="py-3">No requirement</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- SUBSTITUTIONS -->
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-display font-extrabold text-2xl md:text-3xl text-ocean-600 mb-6 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-10 h-10 bg-ocean-500 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center text-white">
              <ArrowLeftRight class="w-5 h-5" />
            </span>
            Substitutions
          </h2>
          <ul class="space-y-4 text-ocean-700 leading-relaxed list-none pl-0">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 text-ocean-500" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M19.04 4.85C17.34 3.2 15.33 2.25 13 2v3.62l9 5.18c-.28-2.3-1.27-4.3-2.96-5.95M12 22c3.44 0 6.16-1.38 8.17-4.14L17.06 16l-8.99 5.2c1.25.53 2.57.8 3.93.8m1-10.59l8.15 4.66c.44-.94.73-1.93.85-2.96l-9-5.18zm-9.12 6.4c.66.91 1.38 1.65 2.17 2.19l8.99-5.1L12 13.15zM11.04 2C10 2.09 9 2.36 8 2.8v10.35l3.04-1.74zM2 12c0 1.39.3 2.77.89 4.12L6 14.28V4c-2.67 2-4 4.65-4 8"/></svg>
              <span>Any player who has paid to participate in the league during the current season may substitute during regular season play. Subs should be reasonably comparable in skill level to the player they are replacing in order to maintain fair and competitive games. Regular season substitutions do not require approval.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- PLAYOFFS -->
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-display font-extrabold text-2xl md:text-3xl text-ocean-600 mb-6 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-10 h-10 bg-ocean-600 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center text-white">
              <Trophy class="w-5 h-5" />
            </span>
            Playoffs
          </h2>
          <ul class="space-y-4 text-ocean-700 leading-relaxed list-none pl-0">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 text-ocean-500" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M19.04 4.85C17.34 3.2 15.33 2.25 13 2v3.62l9 5.18c-.28-2.3-1.27-4.3-2.96-5.95M12 22c3.44 0 6.16-1.38 8.17-4.14L17.06 16l-8.99 5.2c1.25.53 2.57.8 3.93.8m1-10.59l8.15 4.66c.44-.94.73-1.93.85-2.96l-9-5.18zm-9.12 6.4c.66.91 1.38 1.65 2.17 2.19l8.99-5.1L12 13.15zM11.04 2C10 2.09 9 2.36 8 2.8v10.35l3.04-1.74zM2 12c0 1.39.3 2.77.89 4.12L6 14.28V4c-2.67 2-4 4.65-4 8"/></svg>
              <span>Playoff brackets are run in a tournament format, but each bracket's match structure and scoring format may vary based on bracket size and schedule. Depending on the bracket, matches may be a single game to 21 or best-of-three, and scoring may be straight up or win by 2.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 text-ocean-500" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M19.04 4.85C17.34 3.2 15.33 2.25 13 2v3.62l9 5.18c-.28-2.3-1.27-4.3-2.96-5.95M12 22c3.44 0 6.16-1.38 8.17-4.14L17.06 16l-8.99 5.2c1.25.53 2.57.8 3.93.8m1-10.59l8.15 4.66c.44-.94.73-1.93.85-2.96l-9-5.18zm-9.12 6.4c.66.91 1.38 1.65 2.17 2.19l8.99-5.1L12 13.15zM11.04 2C10 2.09 9 2.36 8 2.8v10.35l3.04-1.74zM2 12c0 1.39.3 2.77.89 4.12L6 14.28V4c-2.67 2-4 4.65-4 8"/></svg>
              <span>The same player eligibility and skill-comparability standards from regular season substitutions apply during playoffs, but <strong>playoff substitutions require approval</strong>. Requests must be submitted by <strong>2:00 PM on the day of playoffs</strong> and are subject to a vote by the captains participating in that playoff bracket, with a majority vote determining approval. In the event of a tie, or if a majority of eligible captains do not submit a vote, league organizers will consider the votes received and make the final decision.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 text-ocean-500" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M19.04 4.85C17.34 3.2 15.33 2.25 13 2v3.62l9 5.18c-.28-2.3-1.27-4.3-2.96-5.95M12 22c3.44 0 6.16-1.38 8.17-4.14L17.06 16l-8.99 5.2c1.25.53 2.57.8 3.93.8m1-10.59l8.15 4.66c.44-.94.73-1.93.85-2.96l-9-5.18zm-9.12 6.4c.66.91 1.38 1.65 2.17 2.19l8.99-5.1L12 13.15zM11.04 2C10 2.09 9 2.36 8 2.8v10.35l3.04-1.74zM2 12c0 1.39.3 2.77.89 4.12L6 14.28V4c-2.67 2-4 4.65-4 8"/></svg>
              <span>If substitute requests are denied, teams may still play with the rostered players present, with no minimum female requirements applying for that match.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 text-ocean-500" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M19.04 4.85C17.34 3.2 15.33 2.25 13 2v3.62l9 5.18c-.28-2.3-1.27-4.3-2.96-5.95M12 22c3.44 0 6.16-1.38 8.17-4.14L17.06 16l-8.99 5.2c1.25.53 2.57.8 3.93.8m1-10.59l8.15 4.66c.44-.94.73-1.93.85-2.96l-9-5.18zm-9.12 6.4c.66.91 1.38 1.65 2.17 2.19l8.99-5.1L12 13.15zM11.04 2C10 2.09 9 2.36 8 2.8v10.35l3.04-1.74zM2 12c0 1.39.3 2.77.89 4.12L6 14.28V4c-2.67 2-4 4.65-4 8"/></svg>
              <span>The higher seed gets to choose the serve or the side of the court.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Bottom CTA -->
  <section class="py-16 md:py-20 bg-sand-200">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center">
      <p class="text-ocean-600/80 text-lg italic mb-6">"Because life's too short for bad sets."</p>
      <a
        href="/leagues/"
        class="btn-primary"
      >
        View Leagues & Sign Up
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
